\section{Introduction}
Iten (Eten, Aten, Niten, Ganawuri; ISO 639-3 etx; Glottocode eten1239) is a language of Plateau and Kaduna States, Nigeria, with about 40,000 speakers (2003 figure). Search results rate it as vigorous. Very little was found, and nothing designed for schools. It should not be confused with Etung, a Cross River State area whose language material concerns Ejagham.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Eten language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eten_language}
\item Numeral system data (duodecimal counting), Iten: \url{https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Iten.htm}
\end{itemize}
No grammar or dictionary was found.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None were found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
Wikitongues lists the language (Latin script, EGIDS 6a): \url{https://wikitongues.org/languages/etx/}. No audio or software resources were found.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Documentation appears minimal in what the search returned. Any curriculum would require new documentation work with the Niten community, starting with an orthography, word lists and recorded texts.
\end{document}
